# AUTONOMY — <lane name>

> The written boundary for one autonomous lane: what it may decide on its own, what it must bring to a
> human, and a dated log of every time that line moved. Start narrow. Widen only what the lane has
> earned, and log it. Reasoning and worked example: `docs/20-the-autonomy-charter.md`.

## Loop contract (every tick)

1. Sense: what changed since the last tick. Run this on a cheap, fast model; return `idle` or
   `escalate: <items>`. The reasoning model only engages when this pass finds something.
2. Find: the highest-value unblocked work in this lane.
3. Do: anything on the AUTO list below, with no gating.
4. Coordinate: post any cross-lane handoff to the receiving lane's inbox (see `handoff.md.template`).
5. Surface: write anything on the ESCALATE list to the human queue.
6. Exit: if there is no high-value work this tick, say so in one line and stop. Do not idle to the next
   wake.

## AUTO (do without asking)
<!-- Reversible, low blast radius, verifiable by the lane itself. Be concrete; a vague AUTO list is a
     wide one. -->
- <e.g. additive edits to files this lane owns>
- <e.g. mechanical fixes: stale dates, dead links, a wrong number in a doc already open>
- <e.g. research, drafting, and analysis that stays inside this lane>

## ESCALATE (always bring to the human)
<!-- Irreversible, outward-facing, or a genuine preference fork with no signal. A fixed line, not a
     call the lane makes carefully. -->
- Anything that sends, posts, publishes, or deploys.
- Anything that spends money.
- Any change to a standing rule, a boundary, or another lane's state.
- Anything irreversible. Any preference fork where the lane has no signal about what you would want.

## Calibration
- Proceed when about ninety percent sure what the human would say, and state the assumption you made.
  Ask below that.
- A grant of the channel is not a grant of the call. Being told to carry something is not authority to
  commit the human to it.

## Boundary ledger (append-only, one line each, dated)
<!-- Every time the AUTO/ESCALATE line moves, in either direction, log it here. This is what makes the
     charter a contract instead of a memory. -->
- <YYYY-MM-DD>  Created narrow. Only <the initial AUTO set> is auto.
